A struct whose every field reads from beneath the source's optional struct of
the same name is a copy of it, written only where the instance has it, whether
the author wrote it as a nested body or not. q's nested body renames x and
drops y, so q is a copy of q in both directions. r's nested body adds a
constant, which is written always, and so is r with it. s is dropped whole.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	q?: {
		x?: int
		y?: int
	}
	r?: {
		k?: int
	}
	s?: {
		v?: int
	}
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	q?: {
		x2?: int
	}
	r?: {
		k?: int
		c?: string
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		q: {
			x2: v0_0.q.x
			y:  _drop
		}
		r: {
			c: "z"
		}
		s: _drop
	}
}
